# class: github-templates
# schema: template | trigger-mechanism | label-auto-application | required-fields | ginee-skill-cross-refs | source
# source-glob: .github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/*.{md,yml} + .github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md
# recipe: novel
# authored: 2026-05-23
# Recipe: per template extract trigger mechanism (issue form vs PR form), label auto-application list, required fields, ginee-skill cross-refs.

bug-report.md | Issue form (GitHub issue template with front-matter name/about/title/labels) | labels: [ginee:ready] (auto-applied on issue open from template; D14 inbound trigger) | Required fields: Summary (1-2 sentences), Steps to reproduce (numbered), Expected behavior, Actual behavior (with error/log/screenshot), Affected area (one of: frontend|backend|devops|qa|mobile|ml|data|sre|security|docs|multiple), FR/NFR cited (optional), Acceptance criteria (testable checkbox list), Reporter context (version/env/browser-OS-runtime/frequency) | ginee-pick-up skill on team-lead pickup; qa-engineer owns Acceptance-criteria scenario authoring; solution-architect triage when FR/NFR cited | @.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/bug-report.md
feature-request.md | Issue form (GitHub issue template with front-matter name/about/title/labels) | labels: [ginee:ready] (auto-applied on issue open from template; D14 inbound trigger) | Required fields: Summary (1-2 sentences), Motivation (user pain/business driver/tech-debt), Proposed behavior (observable outcomes not implementation), Affected area (one of: frontend|backend|devops|qa|mobile|ml|data|sre|security|docs|multiple), FR/NFR (with new: prefix for additions; PM dispatches SA for CR/ADR on FR/NFR change), Acceptance criteria (testable checkbox list), Out of scope, References (related issues/discussions/external links) | ginee-pick-up skill on team-lead pickup; solution-architect dispatched by PM when FR/NFR added/changed | @.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/feature-request.md
config.yml | Issue form config (GitHub ISSUE_TEMPLATE config.yml) | n/a (not an issue form; controls template listing behaviour) | blank_issues_enabled: false (forces template selection; no blank issues); contact_links: Report security vulnerability -> GitHub Security Advisories URL | n/a (infrastructure; no ginee skill cross-ref) | @.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/config.yml
PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md | PR form (GitHub pull request description template; markdown with HTML comments as instructions) | n/a (PR templates have no auto-label mechanism) | Required sections: What (imperative-voice change summary), Why (trigger source with reference: TODO/CR/defect/explicit-request), Cites table (Requirement / Architecture-doc section / Mockup section / CR / ADR / Hand-off note — "No source = no PR"), Issue linkage (Closes/Fixes/Related #N for D14 auto-close), Domain breakdown (for cross-domain PRs), Cross-domain sign-offs (SA/backend/frontend/devops/qa/smoke), Cost impact (devops PRs with new resources), Verification log (command + outcome), CI status, Open issues / follow-ups, Out of scope | ginee-address-review skill consumes PR review threads; team-lead populates CI status in automatic-mode (D20); SA + backend + frontend + devops + qa cross-domain sign-offs per process.md | @.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md
